From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 08:11:15 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] mesa/st: hand a driver only the sample mask bits it can use

A sample mask bit past the framebuffer's sample count selects no
sample, but the state tracker handed the driver the whole GL mask.
Zink keys its pipelines on that mask unless the Vulkan driver offers a
dynamic one, and KosmicKrisp cannot: Metal has no fixed-function
sample mask, so the driver folds the mask into the fragment function
and compiles it again for every value. An application that varies the
unused bits therefore paid for a new pipeline and a Metal compile on
every draw. On a four-sample framebuffer that measured 67 ms a draw,
against 0.07 ms for an unchanging mask. The dEQP-GLES31 case
multisample.default_framebuffer.sample_mask_non_effective_bits, which
randomizes those bits for every quad it draws, ran for 48 s and failed
under the 30 s watchdog the Android CTS gives each case.

Keep only the bits that select samples, and pass the full mask when
they select every sample. A driver then sees one value per effective
mask, at most sixteen on four samples, and a mask that covers every
sample stays the mask it was, so a driver that skips its sample mask
work for a full mask, as KosmicKrisp does, still skips it. The update
already runs again whenever the framebuffer changes, because the
sample count is read from it. 512 draws with random unused bits now
take 1.1 s instead of 34 s, the time of sixteen compiles.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/mesa/state_tracker/st_atom_msaa.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mesa/state_tracker/st_atom_msaa.c b/src/mesa/state_tracker/st_atom_msaa.c
index 52c1688fb431a19f667e8b743c9807002ed1ade3..d1e39ef35a536b033ecc67b5b3740d308dd60e95 100644
--- a/src/mesa/state_tracker/st_atom_msaa.c
+++ b/src/mesa/state_tracker/st_atom_msaa.c
@@ -133,6 +133,17 @@ st_update_sample_state(struct st_context *st)
       }
       if (st->ctx->Multisample.SampleMask)
          sample_mask &= st->ctx->Multisample.SampleMaskValue;
+
+      /* A mask bit past the framebuffer's samples has no effect, but a
+       * driver that keys pipeline state on the mask builds a pipeline for
+       * every value of those bits.  Hand it only the bits that select
+       * samples, and the full mask when they select every sample.
+       */
+      const unsigned effective = BITFIELD_MASK(MIN2(sample_count, 32));
+      if ((sample_mask & effective) == effective)
+         sample_mask = 0xffffffff;
+      else
+         sample_mask &= effective;
    }
 
    cso_set_sample_mask(st->cso_context, sample_mask);
